    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4218" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăsymbŏlus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăsum-</span></b> , Fleck.), a,
			um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσύμβολος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that contributes nothing to an entertainment</i>,
				<i>scot-free</i> (in pure Lat., immunis, <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 4,
				12, 23</span></i>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tene asumbolum venire unctum atque lautum e
					balneis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Phorm. 2, 2, 25</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Gell. 6, 13</span></i> (opp.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sumbolam dare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					And. 1, 1, 61</span></i>
			).</div>
